<title>USA: Shuttle Discovery lands in Florida.</title>
<headline>Shuttle Discovery lands in Florida.</headline>
<byline>Steven Young</byline>
<dateline>CAPE CANAVERAL, Fla. 1997-02-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>The space shuttle Discovery soared through a star-filled sky on Friday and touched down at Florida's Kennedy Space Center, ending a 10-day mission to refurbish the Hubble Space Telescope.</p>
<p>The $2 billion reusable spaceship, carrying the seven-man Hubble service crew, glided to a rare nighttime landing at 3:32 a.m. EST (0832 GMT).</p>
